Subject: [PATCH] MilkdropPreset: give feedback reads the reference size's bilinear footprint

Build on 0035 and PR #23's sampler and feedback-history fixes. Above the line reference area, every
bilinear main-texture read of the warp (translated preset shaders and the default warp shader)
reproduces MilkDrop's read on the reference canvas: its reference phase is taken relative to the
pixel's own position (uv_orig), and the four reference-spaced neighbours are blended with MilkDrop's
bilinear weights. The tap distance is solved once per render size on the CPU so that the mean total
variance, including each tap's own native interpolation, is the reference read's f(1-f); on whole-number
scales (2364x1330 is exactly twice the 1182x665 canvas) it is pulled in an eighth of a native texel so
native pixels stay coupled. Per read the GPU computes only a phase and two tap positions, without
branches, so a preset's repeated identical reads stay mergeable; off and phase 0 reduce exactly to the
plain read. Reads at coordinates that do not depend on the pixel's position (stored positions read back
from the frame) stay plain. Point-sampled reads, the composite and the blur textures read the unchanged
frame. The warp's uv/uv_orig varying is highp, as the phase needs sub-texel precision at 4K.

This replaces the uniform (s^2-1)/6 pre-warp blur pass: that over-smoothed identity and texel-aligned
reads every frame (astral spinorgentics encrustcore nz+), took MilkDrop's asymmetric 2-tap shape for a
symmetric one (Royal Mashup 191, Fed quadratrail), filtered only the bilinear input while the blur
levels used the unfiltered frame, and cost a full-screen pass. The rewrite is optional per shader:
a rejected compile falls back to the plain translation. Keep the conservative load-time gate and
the motion-vector minimum scaling while the footprint is active.

Measurements are recorded under docs/superpowers/evidence/0025-feedback-diffusion/.
